## [Dialogue](dialogue)

What the Ash Warren's places say. See the Voice's file for how a place scene works.

### [The First Hollow](ash_hollow_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% The first hollow is a bubble in the rock, round because round is what you get when you dig. Tool marks spiral the walls, and in one place they stop and become writing.

- [Read the writing](ash_hollow_writing) if science ; check science 7 else ash_hollow_scratches, reveal ash_tally, signal ash_tally_found
- [Test the rock](ash_hollow_rock) if engineering ; check engineering 7 else ash_hollow_dull
- [Move on]()

### [A Tally](ash_hollow_writing)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% A tally, cut into the rock at head height for a miner: days worked, loads out, and names crossed off one by one. Beside it, a niche where the tally-keeper kept the stick.

- [Mark it]()

### [Scratches](ash_hollow_scratches)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% Scratches in rows. Somebody meant something by them.

- [Look again](ash_hollow_look)
- [Move on]()

### [What Ran Through the Rock](ash_hollow_rock)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% The rock rings wrong: not ash-field basalt but something denser, threaded with a metal the suits have no name for. They were not mining the rock. They were mining what ran through it.

- [Tell Vex](ash_hollow_vex)
- [Log it]()

### [Vex, on the Rock](ash_hollow_vex)
---
Speaker: chief_vex
---
% Vex. A metal the suit can't name? Get me a sample, even a flake. If it's what I think it is, the refinery would pay for the whole rock.

- [We'll look]()

### [Just Rock](ash_hollow_dull)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_wall_a
---
% Rock. Hard, dark, and saying nothing.

- [Move on]()

### [The Tally-Keeper's Niche](ash_tally_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The tally-keeper's niche: a notched stick, a cup, a lamp gone dark. The last notch is cut deeper than all the rest.

- [Reel the tally in]()

### [The Crossing](ash_crossing_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% Three ways on from the crossing, and two of them are full of rock where the roof came down. The third drops away towards the deep cut - and a slump of rubble is choking even that.

- [Clear the rubble by hand](ash_rubble_free) if engineering ; check engineering 9 else ash_rubble_stuck, open ash_rockfall
- [Blast it with the beam](ash_rubble_cut)
- [Read the demolition scars](ash_crossing_fall) if weapons ; check weapons 7 else ash_crossing_dust, signal ash_fall_read
- [Not yet]()

### [Clear](ash_rubble_free)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The last of the slump slides away into the dark. The way down is open.

- [Down]()

### [It Will Not Shift](ash_rubble_stuck)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% Every rock you move, two more settle into its place. More hands, or the beam.

- [Try again](ash_crossing_look)
- [Leave it]()

### [The Beam](ash_rubble_cut)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% On the Fire app, arm BEAM and select the rubble. It will not argue with the beam.

- [Understood]()

### [Brought Down](ash_crossing_fall)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% The roof did not fall. It was brought down: the drill scars run right to the break. Whoever left last closed two of the ways behind them.

- [Tell Storm](ash_crossing_storm)

### [Storm, on the Fall](ash_crossing_storm)
---
Speaker: prof_storm
---
% They collapsed their own tunnels on the way out? Then whatever they found down there, they did not want it followed. Which, forgive me, is the best possible reason to follow it.

- [Understood]()

### [Dust](ash_crossing_dust)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% Rock dust, settled a long time. It could have fallen any time.

- [Move on]()

### [The Last Room](ash_last_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% The last room is where they stopped, turned round, and left: a bench, a rack of worn-out drill heads, and on the wall a chart cut into a plate that has outlasted everyone who ever read it.

- [Read the chart where it hangs](ash_last_chart) if helm ; check helm 7 else ash_last_blur, signal ash_chart_read
- [Search the bench](ash_last_bench) if comms ; check comms 7 else ash_last_empty, signal ash_letter_found
- [Take the chart and go]()

### [Hidden Twice](ash_last_chart)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% A route chart: the warren, the ash fields, and a line out to a relay somebody has marked with a word the translator gives as "hidden twice".

- [Log it]()

### [Blur](ash_last_blur)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% Lines and marks, and none of them lining up with anything you know. Try it from further back.

- [Try again](ash_last_look)
- [Move on]()

### [A Letter](ash_last_bench)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% A letter, never sent, under the drill heads: "We found where it runs. We are closing the ways behind us. If you are reading this, leave it where it is."

- [Leave the letter]()

### [Drill Heads](ash_last_empty)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_obelisk
---
% Drill heads, worn to stubs. Nothing else on the bench.

- [Look again](ash_last_look)
- [Move on]()

### [The Seam](ash_seam_look)
---
Backdrop: pic:cv_rubble
---
% A seam of the dense metal, cut back and left where they dropped their tools.

- [Ask Eddy](ash_seam_eddy) if comms
- [Haul it later]()

### [Eddy, on Deep Ore](ash_seam_eddy)
---
Speaker: crazy_eddy
---
% Deep ore? From the ash fields? My friend, nobody mines the ash fields, which is why nobody has any, which is why I will pay you anything. Within reason. Mostly.

- [We'll see]()

